{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moshe said, when HaShem gives you.</b> This is the same statement he began with, but because of the length of the matter he repeats it, and likewise he explained: 'in the evening, and you shall know, when HaShem gives you' — in the evening meat, and 'in the morning, and you shall see, when HaShem gives you' — in the morning bread. <b>Not against us are your complaints.</b> You directed the complaint against us when you said, 'for you brought us out.' Yet it is revealed and known that your complaint was not aimed [at us], but rather upward, as it were, like a person who complains about a dignitary and directs his complaint at the attendant — and the dignitary knows that the complaint is really against him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:10.841635109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}